# Field of view

Your character has a limited viewing angle: you clearly see what is in front of you and right around you, while everything behind your back transitions into a desaturated area with a grain effect.

Below you can adjust the graininess outside your field of view (this option can also be changed later in "Options" -> "Accessibility").

<GuideCard>
  <GuideCVarSlider CVar="vision.grain_scale" Title="Vision cone graininess" Min="0" Max="1" Format="Percent" DisabledByCVar="accessibility.reduced_motion" Note="At 0%, the area behind you stays pure black-and-white without noise. Enabling 'Reduce motion of visual effects' also disables graininess." DisabledNote="The slider is disabled because 'Reduce motion of visual effects' is currently enabled in Options."/>
</GuideCard>

